  "notes": [
    "Seven lineage variants, not every historical training revision. Historical Qwen3 4B is separate from current Qwen3.5 4B.",
    "Prototype0.5 head lacks base revision; runtime explicitly pins currently published Qwen2.5 base. This is not a claim of recovered historical training revision.",
    "Checkpoint temperatures read without executing pickle, via pickletools; missing temperature defaults1.0 per upstream Meta.",
    "Source/weights/base must be pinned; response model echoes caller and does not prove identity.",
    "No quantization. bf16 is serving default, not exactfp32 evaluation path. Calibration may not transfer to Keating.",
    "Retain base-image numpy/scipy compatibility; numpy2.5.3 is upstream lockfile metadata, not required for the isolated inference imports. No datasets/scikit-learn training imports needed.",
    "Uniform prefix cache size1 uses official exact state-prefix reuse: hybrid models compute a state once per request instead of repeating it for every question. No context/question change.",
    "Runtime exception: observed GPU image torch2.9.0+cu129 is pinned as2.9.0 (CUDA local suffix recorded in receipts). Upstream source pyproject declares torch>=2.6,<2.9 and lockfile2.8.0; this run intentionally retains image CUDA/Torch stack. Actual inference, not dependency installation, establishes operational compatibility. Weights/source unchanged."
